# SYNTHETIC — hand-written from RFC 1939, not a recording.
# The phase-0 capture against a real server has not happened yet.
# SPLIT delivers each line of the RETR response one byte at a time, including
# the dot-stuffed body line. A machine that only accepts whole lines deadlocks.

S: +OK POP3 server ready
C: RETR 2
SPLIT
S: +OK 10 octets
SPLIT
S: Hello
SPLIT
S: ..dot
SPLIT
S: .
C: QUIT
S: +OK bye
DONE
